menu "sys_device_policy"

    config SYS_DEVICE_POLICY_QUEUE_BYTES
        int "Queue (bytes)"
        default 1024
        range 256 8192
        help
          Room of the ring buffer for the reported errors that wait for the
          policy's task, each as a record (the buffer's 8 B and the record).
          Only an error that needs a response is queued. A full buffer fails
          the report with ERR_DEV_FAULT_RESPONSE (stage QUEUE). A multiple
          of 4, at least twice the largest record.

    config SYS_DEVICE_POLICY_TASK_PRIO
        int "Task priority"
        default 14
        range 1 24
        help
          The task that stops the VM and suspends every device on a critical
          error: above the event task (6) and the router work task (5), so
          the safe state is not kept waiting by them; below the urgent task
          (15).

    config SYS_DEVICE_POLICY_TASK_STACK
        int "Task stack (bytes)"
        default 4096
        range 3072 32768
        help
          Runs the responses: the sweep of every device (their suspend()
          hooks, I2C), a device's SUSPEND or RESET, the action runner.

endmenu
